{#- The callout, one of the canonical components.

    `role="complementary"` and `aria-label` are the accessibility contract: the
    box is an aside about the surrounding prose, and a screen reader announces
    it by its title. The title is repeated as visible text because the label is
    not rendered.

    `data-canonical` and `data-part` are the markup contract: the landmarks
    every conforming theme's callout carries, whatever its classes.

    The manifest declares `body: markdown`, so the body arrives between blank
    lines: the raw-HTML block the opening element starts closes before the
    body, and the body reaches the markdown parser whole. Keep the closing tag
    in column 0 -- after a blank line, an indented `</div>` is an indented
    code block.
-#}
{%- set type = attrs.type | default("info") -%}
{%- set title = attrs.title | default(type | capitalize) -%}
{%- if attrs.collapsible -%}
<details class="callout callout-{{ type }}" role="complementary" aria-label="{{ title }}" data-canonical="callout"><summary class="callout-title" data-part="title">{{ title }}</summary>
{{ body }}
</details>
{%- else -%}
<div class="callout callout-{{ type }}" role="complementary" aria-label="{{ title }}" data-canonical="callout"><p class="callout-title" data-part="title">{{ title }}</p>
{{ body }}
</div>
{%- endif -%}
